%N A402130 Number of plane partitions of n with equal corresponding row and column sums.
%C A402130 For every i, the sum of row i must equal the sum of column i. Zero border rows and columns are omitted, so every nonempty counted plane partition is square. Repeated rows and columns are allowed.
%C A402130 Every symmetric plane partition satisfies this condition, but nonsymmetric ones can also satisfy it. A plane partition and its transpose are counted separately when they differ.
%C A402130 Every nonempty counted matrix is the adjacency matrix of a directed multigraph with n arcs, allowing loops and parallel arcs, in which every vertex has equal indegree and outdegree. The vertices are ordered so that the adjacency matrix is a plane partition. Every vertex has arcs to and from the first vertex, so the digraph admits an Euler circuit.
%H A402130 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A402130/b402130.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..70</a>
%e A402130 The nonsymmetric plane partition [[3,2,2],[3,1,0],[1,1,0]] is counted by a(13): both its row sums and its column sums are 7,4,2. Its transpose is also counted.
%Y A402130 Cf. A000219, A005987.
